{"name":"Mauve Aquarelle","hex":"#e3d2db","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mauve","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A rich purple synthetic dye, which faded easily, briefly popular c. 1859‒1873 and now called mauveine.","A pale purple or violet colour, like the colour of the dye after it has faded."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a pale purple colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mauve"},{"term":"aquarelle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A watercolour (painting)","A printed picture coloured by the application of watercolour through stencils, using a different stencil for each colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aquarelle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mauve","blocks":[{"text":"Mauve is a pale purple color named after the mallow flower. The first use of the word mauve as a color was in 1796–1798 according to the Oxford English Dictionary, but its use seems to have been rare before 1859. Another name for the color is mallow, with the first recorded use of mallow as a color name in English in 1611."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Wilde_Malve.JPG/330px-Wilde_Malve.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mauve","wikidata":"Q604079"},{"title":"Watercolor painting","blocks":[{"text":"Watercolor or watercolour, also aquarelle, is a painting method in which the paints are made of pigments suspended in a water-based solution. Watercolor refers to both the medium and the resulting artwork."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Dolceacqua43_-_Artista_locale_mentre_dipinge_un_acquarello.jpg/330px-Dolceacqua43_-_Artista_locale_mentre_dipinge_un_acquarello.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Watercolor_painting","wikidata":"Q50030"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Loves_Messenger_Stillman_DAM.jpg/500px-Loves_Messenger_Stillman_DAM.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Loves_Messenger_Stillman_DAM.jpg/1280px-Loves_Messenger_Stillman_DAM.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Loves_Messenger_Stillman_DAM.jpg/500px-Loves_Messenger_Stillman_DAM.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Love's Messenger, an 1885 watercolor and tempera by Marie Spartali Stillman","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALoves_Messenger_Stillman_DAM.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Albrecht_D%C3%BCrer_-_Hare%2C_1502_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/500px-Albrecht_D%C3%BCrer_-_Hare%2C_1502_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Albrecht_D%C3%BCrer_-_Hare%2C_1502_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/1280px-Albrecht_D%C3%BCrer_-_Hare%2C_1502_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Albrecht_D%C3%BCrer_-_Hare%2C_1502_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/500px-Albrecht_D%C3%BCrer_-_Hare%2C_1502_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Albrecht Dürer, Young Hare, 1502, watercolor and body color, Albertina, Vienna","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAlbrecht_D%C3%BCrer_-_Hare%2C_1502_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Thomas_Girtin_006.JPG/330px-Thomas_Girtin_006.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Th